# swift-os boot services. One allowlisted token per line.
# swos-init runs each as a child (a sibling of the login shell) and reaps them;
# use `crond-supervised` instead of `crond` to have it restarted if it crashes.
# inputd is the C5j userland virtio-input driver: it owns the keyboard the kernel
# no longer drives and injects keystrokes into the tty. On a board with no
# virtio-input device it exits cleanly (a no-op), so it is safe to list always.
inputd
sshd
crond
